UPSTREAM SOURCES

  Geoscience Australia: Digital Elevation Model (DEM) of Australia derived from LiDAR 5 Metre Grid (2015,
  https://doi.org/10.26186/89644). © Commonwealth of Australia (Geoscience Australia), Creative Commons Attribution
  4.0. Read through Mapterhorn's terrain tiles (https://mapterhorn.com, attribution at mapterhorn.com/attribution) as
  copied by Plotlay. Changes: resampled to Web Mercator and rounded to 0.125 m (zoom 14) and 0.25 m (zoom 13) by
  Mapterhorn; cut to the study area and written as GeoTIFF by Plotlay (data/heights/).

  G-NAF (Geocoded National Address File), August 2026 release. Incorporates or developed using G-NAF © Geoscape
  Australia licensed by the Commonwealth of Australia under the Open Geo-coded National Address File (G-NAF) End
  User Licence Agreement (https://data.gov.au/dataset/geocoded-national-address-file-g-naf). The licence grants the
  rights of CC BY 4.0 with one restriction: G-NAF must not be used to generate an address or a compilation of
  addresses for the sending of mail unless each address has been verified against another source.
  Changes: addresses counted by level and suburb; no address list is published.

  Australian Bureau of Statistics: Australian Statistical Geography Standard (ASGS) Edition 3 mesh blocks and
  suburbs and localities (2021); Census of Population and Housing 2021, Mesh Block Counts. Creative Commons
  Attribution 4.0. Based on Australian Bureau of Statistics data.
  Changes: mesh blocks simplified by 2.5 m and joined to their counts; residents shared by area under each level.

  Government of South Australia, Department for Housing and Urban Development: Land Use Generalised 2025
  (data.sa.gov.au), Creative Commons Attribution 4.0. Changes: cut to the study area; area under each level by class
  (data/tables/levels_landuse.csv).

  OpenStreetMap roads, © OpenStreetMap contributors, Open Database Licence 1.0 (see levels_roads.csv above).

  The levels come from published figures: the SA Coast Protection Board's Policy Document (revised October 2022),
  the highest astronomical tide at Outer Harbor and its chart datum (Bureau of Meteorology; Tonkin Consulting 2014;
  Department for Environment and Heritage 2005), listed with links in data/tables/sources.csv.

  The map pictures in visuals/ are drawn over Plotlay's Quiet base map, made from OpenStreetMap: © OpenStreetMap
  contributors (ODbL), tiles Protomaps. They are produced works and credit it.

